# Visual Studio 2015/2017 cache/options directory
.vs/
# Uncomment if you have tasks that create the project's static files in wwwroot
#wwwroot/

# Aerie.Web build output - Aerie.Web is the source of truth; this is
# regenerated by `dotnet build`/Docker on every build (see Aerie.Api.csproj's
# BuildDashboard/BuildHome targets and Dockerfile.api).
src/Aerie.Api/wwwroot/apps/

# `tsc -b` output for the two apps whose tsconfig.node.json is still a
# `composite` project (admin, docs). These were committed once and became a
# trap: Vite's config lookup tries vite.config.js *before* vite.config.ts, so
# a stale compiled copy silently shadows the TypeScript file everyone edits -
# an edit to vite.config.ts would build fine and change nothing. Found on
# 2026-08-29 when exactly that happened. Those projects now emit into
# node_modules/.tmp/node-build instead, so these should never reappear;
# ignored so that they cannot.
src/Aerie.Web/apps/*/vite.config.js
src/Aerie.Web/apps/*/vite.config.d.ts
src/Aerie.Web/apps/*/tsconfig.node.tsbuildinfo

