# but database connection strings (with potential passwords) will be unencrypted
*.pubxml
*.publishproj

# Microsoft Azure Web App publish settings. Comment the next line if you want to
# checkin your Azure Web App publish settings, but sensitive information contained
# in these scripts will be unencrypted
PublishScripts/

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg
# The packages folder can be ignored because of Package Restore
**/[Pp]ackages/*
# except build/, which is used as an MSBuild target.
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
# ...and except the npm workspace packages, which are source. This NuGet rule
# is a path glob, not a NuGet-aware one, so it swallowed src/Aerie.Web/packages/
# silently - `git add` reported nothing and `git status` stayed clean. Anything
# new under a directory called "packages" wants a `git check-ignore` first.
!src/Aerie.Web/packages/
!src/Aerie.Web/packages/**
# Uncomment if necessary however generally it will be regenerated when needed
#!**/[Pp]ackages/repositories.config
# NuGet v3's project.json files produces more ignorable files
*.nuget.props
*.nuget.targets

# Microsoft Azure Build Output
csx/
*.build.csdef

# Microsoft Azure Emulator
ecf/
rcf/

# Windows Store app package directories and files
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
Package.StoreAssociation.xml
_pkginfo.txt
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload

# Visual Studio cache files
# files ending in .cache can be ignored
*.[Cc]ache
# but keep track of directories ending in .cache
!?*.[Cc]ache/

# Others
ClientBin/
~$*
*~
*.dbmdl
*.dbproj.schemaview
*.jfm
*.pfx
*.publishsettings
orleans.codegen.cs

# Including strong name files can present a security risk
# (https://github.com/github/gitignore/pull/2483#issue-259490424)
#*.snk

# Since there are multiple workflows, uncomment next line to ignore bower_components
# (https://github.com/github/gitignore/pull/1529#issuecomment-104372622)
#bower_components/

# RIA/Silverlight projects
Generated_Code/

# Backup & report files from converting an old project file
# to a newer Visual Studio version. Backup files are not needed,
# because we have git ;-)
_UpgradeReport_Files/
Backup*/
# ...but `Backup*/` is unanchored and, on a case-insensitive checkout
# (core.ignorecase=true, i.e. every macOS clone), it also matches
# containers/backup/ — the restic backup container's real source. Git won't
# descend into an excluded directory, so the directory itself has to be
# re-included here, not just its contents.
!containers/backup/
# ...and deploy/cluster/data/backup/, the Phase 8 backup tenant, for exactly
# the same reason. Found the hard way: the 8b.4 commit that added that
# directory landed only the ../schema/kustomization.yaml line pointing at it,
# so HEAD referenced a base git had never been shown and `kubectl kustomize
# deploy/cluster/data/schema` failed on a fresh clone while building fine in
# the working tree. Any new directory literally named `backup` needs a line
# here.
!deploy/cluster/data/backup/
UpgradeLog*.XML
UpgradeLog*.htm
ServiceFabricBackup/
*.rptproj.bak

